\\]\n\\[ 81 = \\triangle b^2 + \\Box b + \\Box \\]\n\nSince the right-hand sides of these equations are all the same, we can equate the left-hand sides to each other:\n\n\\[ 36 = \\triangle b^2 + \\Box b + \\Box \\]\n\\[ 64 = \\triangle b^2 + \\Box b + \\Box \\]\n\\[ 81 = \\triangle b^2 + \\Box b + \\Box \\]\n\nSubtracting the first equation from the second, we get:\n\n\\[ 64 - 36 = (\\triangle b^2 + \\Box b + \\Box) - (\\triangle b^2 + \\Box b + \\Box) \\]\n\\[ 28 = \\triangle b^2 + \\Box b + \\Box - \\triangle b^2 - \\Box b - \\Box \\]\n\\[ 28 = 0 \\]\n\nThis is not possible, so we need to re-evaluate the approach. Instead, let's try to find a base \\( b \\) such that the numbers 36, 64, and 81 can be represented by the same three-digit number in base \\( b \\). We will test different bases to see if we can find a match.\n\nFirst, let's try base 8:\n\n\\[ 36_{10} = 44_8 \\]\n\\[ 64_{10} = 100_8 \\]\n\\[ 81_{10} = 121_8 \\]\n\nThese do not match. Let's try base 9:\n\n\\[ 36_{10} = 40_9 \\]\n\\[ 64_{10} = 71_9 \\]\n\\[ 81_{10} = 100_9 \\]\n\nThese do not match. Let's try base 10:\n\n\\[ 36_{10} = 36_{10} \\]\n\\[ 64_{10} = 64_{10} \\]\n\\[ 81_{10} = 81_{10} \\]\n\nThese do not match. Let's try base 11:\n\n\\[ 36_{10} = 33_{11} \\]\n\\[ 64_{10} = 59_{11} \\]\n\\[ 81_{10} = 74_{11} \\]\n\nThese do not match. Let's try base 12:\n\n\\[ 36_{10} = 30_{12} \\]\n\\[ 64_{10} = 54_{12} \\]\n\\[ 81_{10} = 69_{12} \\]\n\nThese do not match. Let's try base 13:\n\n\\[ 36_{10} = 2A_{13} \\]\n\\[ 64_{10} = 4C_{13} \\]\n\\[ 81_{10} = 63_{13} \\]\n\nThese do not match. Let's try base 14:\n\n\\[ 36_{10} = 28_{14} \\]\n\\[ 64_{10} = 48_{14} \\]\n\\[ 81_{10} = 5B_{14} \\]\n\nThese do not match. Let's try base 15:\n\n\\[ 36_{10} = 26_{15} \\]\n\\[ 64_{10} = 44_{15} \\]\n\\[ 81_{10} = 56_{15} \\]\n\nThese do not match. Let's try base 16:\n\n\\[ 36_{10} = 24_{16} \\]\n\\[ 64_{10} = 40_{16} \\]\n\\[ 81_{10} = 51_{16} \\]\n\nThese do not match. Let's try base 17:\n\n\\[ 36_{10} = 22_{17} \\]\n\\[ 64_{10} = 3D_{17} \\]\n\\[ 81_{10} = 4D_{17} \\]\n\nThese do not match. Let's try base 18:\n\n\\[ 36_{10} = 20_{18} \\]\n\\[ 64_{10} = 38_{18} \\]\n\\[ 81_{10} = 45_{18} \\]\n\nThese do not match. Let's try base 19:\n\n\\[ 36_{10} = 1H_{19} \\]\n\\[ 64_{10} = 37_{19} \\]\n\\[ 81_{10} = 45_{19} \\]\n\nThese do not match. Let's try base 20:\n\n\\[ 36_{10} = 1G_{20} \\]\n\\[ 64_{10} = 34_{20} \\]\n\\[ 81_{10} = 41_{20} \\]\n\nThese do not match. Let's try base 21:\n\n\\[ 36_{10} = 1F_{21} \\]\n\\[ 64_{10} = 31_{21} \\]\n\\[ 81_{10} = 3C_{21} \\]\n\nThese do not match. Let's try base 22:\n\n\\[ 36_{10} = 1E_{22} \\]\n\\[ 64_{10} = 2O_{22} \\]\n\\[ 81_{10} = 39_{22} \\]\n\nThese do not match. Let's try base 23:\n\n\\[ 36_{10} = 1D_{23} \\]\n\\[ 64_{10} = 2K_{23} \\]\n\\[ 81_{10} = 36_{23} \\]\n\nThese do not match. Let's try base 24:\n\n\\[ 36_{10} = 1C_{24} \\]\n\\[ 64_{10} = 2H_{24} \\]\n\\[ 81_{10} = 39_{24} \\]\n\nThese do not match. Let's try base 25:\n\n\\[ 36_{10} = 1B_{25} \\]\n\\[ 64_{10} = 2J_{25} \\]\n\\[ 81_{10} = 36_{25} \\]\n\nThese do not match. Let's try base 26:\n\n\\[ 36_{10} = 1A_{26} \\]\n\\[ 64_{10} = 28_{26} \\]\n\\[ 81_{10} = 33_{26} \\]\n\nThese match. Therefore, the value of \\(\\triangle\\Box\\Box\\) is \\(\\boxed{333}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{333}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
